# Thornswood, the one door on 443.
#
# This is the reference copy and it matches the live one as of 18 September.
# The live one is C:\Thornswood-Caddy\Caddyfile on the VPS. Setup-Domain.ps1
# sends this file (since 25 September, issue #543), so a new box gets exactly
# this; an edit made on the box by hand is lost the next time it runs, so make
# it here. It lived only on the box until 18 September, which meant the only
# record of how the site was reachable was the box itself.
#
# Caddy gets the certificate and renews it on its own. The email below is what
# Let's Encrypt writes to if one is about to lapse.
#
# Keep it in caddy fmt shape. `caddy fmt --overwrite .\Caddyfile` does it, and
# validate complains about the line if you do not.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE VOICE BLOCKS ARE THE ONLY WAY TO VOICE.
#
# The voice services listen on 127.0.0.1:7778 and 127.0.0.1:7789 only, and
# every client uses https://thornswood.net/voice and /voice-dev with wss for
# the socket. The three steps this block once listed are done: the clients
# build wss and nothing else, they went out, and the services bind loopback,
# the default since #1304. A join token and a Discord ticket only ever reach
# the service through here: it refuses one over plain http or ws, and Caddy
# marks what it carries with X-Forwarded-Proto https.
#
# handle_path strips the prefix, so /voice/health reaches the service as
# /health and everything it serves keeps working unchanged. Caddy carries a
# WebSocket upgrade through reverse_proxy without being told to, so the
# signalling socket needs nothing more than this. Take these blocks out
# (Setup-Domain.ps1 writes a Caddyfile without them) and voice is gone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

{
	email datdude365d@gmail.com
	storage file_system C:/Thornswood-Caddy/data
}

thornswood.net, www.thornswood.net {
	encode gzip

	handle_path /voice/* {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:7778
	}

	handle_path /voice-dev/* {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:7789
	}
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3001
}
